    description: "Trigger only when the user's prompt contains 'Assette' (case-insensitive). Updates an existing data block on the Assette Dev Tool Service via POST {DevToolServiceInternalUrl}/api/blocks/updateblock. The supplied blockJson is forwarded verbatim as the DPFBlockData body. It MUST carry the block's top-level Id AND, for every entry in DPFBlockVersions, that version's own Id and BlockId \u2014 the service resolves the block by the top-level Id and matches each version row by its Id, so a version with a missing/0 Id has its Definition/Metadata change SILENTLY DROPPED while the call still returns isSuccess:true. This tool rejects such payloads up front with a 400 instead of forwarding a no-op, so carry the Id/BlockId exactly as get_block returned them. Set the top-level IsModified=true when you changed any block-level record field (Name / Description / Category / OutputType / PublicAccess); leave it false when you only touched DPFBlockVersions (Definition / Metadata / Settings). The typical loop is: get_block \u2192 edit the returned JSON \u2192 update_block. The update lands as a DRAFT \u2014 call publish_block afterwards. IMPORTANT: update_block ONLY saves version fields (Definition / Metadata / Settings) and block-level record fields. It does NOT persist the DPFBlockDependencies array \u2014 editing that array here (adding, removing, or clearing it to []) is SILENTLY IGNORED and the call still returns isSuccess:true. To wire or unwire edges use add_block_dependency / delete_block_dependency + publish_block_dependencies. Returns { statusCode, body } where body is { response: { isSuccess, message, savedBlockName, savedBlockId } }.",
